BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Readers' Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T180000
UID:6a905dcaa942147a586336df@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:2nd & 4th Tuesdays\, 2-4 pm in the OCA Lobby\nInterested in le
 arning\, sharing and reading short plays? Readers Theatre is a fun opportu
 nity to express yourself.\nReaders Theatre participants read scripts adapt
 ed from literature\, while the ‘audience’ pictures the action by heari
 ng the script being read aloud. It requires no sets\, costumes\, props\, o
 r memorized lines. Instead of acting literature as in a play\, the perform
 er’s goal is to read a script aloud effectively\, enabling the audience 
 to visualize the action. Performers bring the text alive by using voice\, 
 facial expressions\, and some gestures. $15 participation fee\, $10 for OC
 A members.\nAlternating READER’S CHOICE nights: Can be play\, poetry\, s
 tory\, essay\, your own writing\, OR ??????\nFor more information\, email\
 nJoan Ambrosini\,\ncoordinator .
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/readers-the
 atre-2-m26cd
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
