BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gravenstein Mandolin Ensemble
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T210000
UID:6a8c96854c64ae20c92e6649@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the bright\, shimmering sound of strings in harmony
  as the\nGravenstein Mandolin Ensemble\ntakes the stage at Occidental Cent
 er for the Arts. This talented local ensemble brings together mandolins\, 
 mandolas\, mandocello\, and guitar for a lively musical journey spanning f
 olk traditions\, classical favorites\, contemporary arrangements\, and mel
 odies from around the world.\nWith the mandolin family’s distinctive ble
 nd of warmth\, sparkle\, and rhythmic energy\, the ensemble creates a soun
 d that is both intimate and wonderfully full. Join us for an afternoon of 
 beautiful music\, community\, and the irresistible charm of many mandolins
  making music together!\nGet Tickets\nThe Gravenstein Mandolin Ensemble\nw
 as formed in 2006 in Sebastopol\, California\, a town famous for its Grave
 nstein apples. With humble beginnings\, the six original members grew to i
 ts present size of fifteen\, including the entire mandolin family: mandoli
 ns\, mandolas\, mandocellos\, with additional support from guitar and bass
 . The repertoire includes music from the Classical Era to the most contemp
 orary works for modern mandolins\; the geographical range includes music f
 rom Italy\, Spain\, Germany\, Eastern Europe as well as Latin America. Sma
 ller groups\, or “breakout” ensembles\, often perform a variety of mus
 ic\, including Bluegrass\, Celtic\, Choro\, and more. The GME has performe
 d at the Green Center at Sonoma State University\, the San Francisco Mando
 lin Festival and numerous venues through the North Bay Area. In 2018\, the
  GME co-hosted the national convention of the Classical Mandolin Associati
 on of America\, held in Santa Rosa.\nJohn Metras\, Music Director\nGus Gar
 elick\, Concertmaster\nFirst Mandolins:\nEd Hance\nDana Trillo\nSecond Man
 dolins:\nChris Eccles\nBob Baeyen\nEddie Guthman\nRich Nosker\nElla Smith\
 nMandolas:\nDan Baron\nDave Cohen\nJan Kahdeman\nMandocellos:\nRhonda Bern
 ey\nJan Hansen\nGuitar:\nJohn Metras\nBass:\nDorian Bartley
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/gravenstein
 -mandolin-ensemble
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
